224 0 obj
  << /ActualText (A\056 Experience Proposal \046 Justification\n\nOpportunity Identified from Assignment 2\n\nOur original Patterns of Time experience was a digital interactive story game where youths took on the role of a batik apprentice and made choices that shaped their journey while learning about batik and cultural preservation\056 Through developing the experience\054 we identified an opportunity to make the learning experience more immersive by moving beyond digital storytelling and allowing users to physically interact with the craft\056 While the original experience successfully used storytelling\054 choice and gamification to encourage engagement\054 the experience was primarily centred around the temporary campaign and had limited purpose for users once the story was completed\056 There was also no clear pathway for users to discover or purchase Heritage Bay products\056\nThis presented an opportunity to create an experience that could connect heritage learning\054 hands\055on participation\054 artisan stories and Heritage Bay\047s products while giving the digital platform a longer\055term purpose\056\n\nProposed Experience\n\nWe propose evolving Patterns of Time into a physical\055first phygital apprenticeship experience\056 Visitors take on the role of an apprentice and move through a series of physical stations where they discover batik patterns\054 learn about traditional tools and processes\054 hear stories from artisans and participate in hands\055on activities\056 Users receive a digital Apprentice Card through the Heritage Bay app\054 which is scanned at each station to track their progress throughout the apprenticeship\056\nThe physical experience is supported and extended by the app\056 Users can scan QR codes to discover artisan stories\054 complete interactive activities\054 upload their own batik designs and see them brought to life through projection mapping\056 After completing the physical apprenticeship\054 users can continue exploring the original Patterns of Time story game\054 discover more artisan stories and browse or purchase Heritage Bay products either through the app or in person\056\n\nHow the Proposal Builds Upon Insights from Assignment 2\n\nThe refined experience builds upon the strengths of our original concept rather than replacing it\056 Assignment 2 showed us that interactive storytelling\054 choice\054 gamification and personalisation could make heritage learning more engaging for younger audiences\056 We retained these elements through the Patterns of Time story game\054 progress tracking and interactive digital content\054 but repositioned them within a broader experience\056\n\nWe also recognised that batik is a craft that can be better understood through active participation rather than digital consumption alone\056 The refined experience therefore introduces physical touchpoints where users can see\054 touch and learn about batik tools and processes before creating something of their own\056 This creates a stronger connection between the digital content and the physical craft\056\n\nAnother key improvement is the role of the app\056 Rather than creating a temporary campaign\055specific app with limited use after the experience ends\054 the app is positioned as a longer\055term Heritage Bay platform\056 The campaign becomes one layer of the platform\054 while artisan stories and product discovery give users additional reasons to return\056 The addition of a product purchase pathway also creates a clearer connection between learning about batik and discovering the products and artisans represented by Heritage Bay\056\n\nValue for Heritage Bay and Its Users\n\nFor users\054 the experience provides a more engaging and meaningful way to learn about batik by allowing them to learn through doing\056 Instead of only reading about cultural heritage\054 they can discover the stories behind patterns\054 understand traditional tools and processes\054 interact with artisan stories and create their own designs\056 The combination of physical and digital touchpoints also allows users to continue their journey beyond the physical experience through stories\054 the Patterns of Time game and product exploration\056\n\nFor Heritage Bay\054 the experience provides a stronger way to engage younger audiences while supporting its role in preserving and promoting Indonesian cultural heritage\056 By connecting artisan stories and cultural knowledge with hands\055on participation\054 the experience can make batik more accessible and relevant to a younger generation\056 The integrated product pathway also allows users to naturally move from learning about the craft \222 understanding its value \222 discovering the products and artisans behind it\056\n\nMost importantly\054 the refined direction transforms Patterns of Time from a primarily temporary digital campaign into a longer\055term phygital Heritage Bay experience\056 The physical apprenticeship creates an immersive entry point\054 while the app provides opportunities for continued storytelling\054 discovery and purchase beyond the initial visit\056 This creates value not only during the campaign\054 but also through an ongoing relationship between users\054 artisans and Heritage Bay\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 223 0 R
     /Pg 220 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
